200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 171 0 R
/E (While Philippine barangays are legally mandated by DILG MC No. 2017-144 to operate active Violence Against Women \(VAW\) Desks, Barangay Lepa still suffers from an "analog lag" caused by manual, paper-based incident logging. This manual system creates a critical socio-technical void marked by fragmented data, slow processing times for life-saving Barangay Protection Orders \(BPOs\), and desk-bound limitations for on-the-move responders. Furthermore, the lack of private reporting channels reinforces a dangerous "culture of silence" among victims due to social stigma and fear of retaliation. To bridge this gap, this study develops BrgyAlert, a mobile-first platform that integrates a secure cloud backend with an AI-driven risk stratification engine. By leveraging Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) to automatically triage situational urgency into Low, Medium, or High-risk levels, BrgyAlert eliminates administrative bias, protects victim confidentiality, and transitions grassroots local governance into a proactive, data-driven safety ecosystem.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
